{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He said, etc., What is this in your hand?</b> This question is not like HaShem's question to Balaam (Numbers 22:9) ״מִי הָאֲנָשִׁים״ etc., and they of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 19) that He found him [to be like] a vessel of urinary water, for He should have said, 'You know' — for there, the meaning of the question is that the matter is hidden and He asks about it, and from what one answers one reveals one's mind — that it is a vessel of urinary water — whereas this question did not ask about something hidden, for it was known that he had a staff in his hand; rather, it was like one who wants him to acknowledge the matter with his own mouth. And Moses fulfilled his Master's command: <b>And he said, A staff</b> — and the construal of the meaning is: 'and he said' — you discern what you are holding in your hand, what it is; and he said to Him, 'Behold, my Master, I recognize what is in my hand — it is a staff.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:17.249925368Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}